# NEG (Round XXV Track B — one-sided-combinator class): Option.unwrap_error
# does NOT exist in the phase-0 subset. Ratified Result-only per
# `docs/language-reference.md:3861-3891` (Option has one payload; no Error
# to unwrap).
#
# Pre-fix (RED-verified 2026-08-02): Rust `gg check` prints "OK: no semantic
# errors" then `gg build` crashes at C-compile with `incompatible types`;
# ggdef `run` REJECTED at eval-time via the WEAKER generic fallthrough
# ("`.unwrap_error()` on enum") that doesn't carry the ratified reject
# code — too late for corpus_b `CheckFails` adjudication and imprecise.
# Core #8 both-wrong class.
#
# Post-fix: ggdef `elaborate_method` REJECTS at elaborate-time with
# `error[E_NoMethodFound]: `.unwrap_error()` on Option is outside the
# phase-0 subset (Result-only)`. Rust-side class-fix owed as HIGH
# follow-up (test #[ignore]d until Rust ships reject at semantic layer).

void main():
    Option[int] o = Some(5)
    int x = o.unwrap_error()
    print(x)
